# Dependencies & build
node_modules
dist/

# Python bytecode cache (e.g. scripts/hooks/__pycache__/*.pyc)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Runtime self-modified file: the agent rewrites HEARTBEAT.md every heartbeat
# tick, so it is a runtime artifact, not source. Phase 1 (this line) makes new
# clones ignore it; phase 2 (`git rm --cached HEARTBEAT.md`, once the update.sh
# pre-pull reset-guard is deployed fleet-wide) drops it from tracking for good.
HEARTBEAT.md

# Secrets & personal data
# GITIGNENV820: editor backups / copies of .env (.env~, .env.bak, .env.local)
# were not covered -- only the exact name was. Cover every variant, keep the
# tracked example file. *~ catches editor backups of ANY secret-bearing file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*~
store/*
# Ingatlan (personal real-estate market tracker, Peti 2026-08-12): scraped listing
# data, OAuth tokens/session, and DB files are personal runtime data, not source --
# code (scraper/analysis/webapp) under Ingatlan/ stays tracked as usual.
Ingatlan/data/
Ingatlan/*.db
Ingatlan/*.sqlite*
Ingatlan/.env
Ingatlan/.credentials/
Ingatlan/token*
# Operational scripts under store/ ARE version-controlled (code, not runtime data).
# Everything else in store/ (DB, tokens, state JSON) stays ignored.
!store/*.sh
# ...and .py, which the rule above always meant: store/cleancore-landed-check.py is tracked only
# because someone force-added it, so the next operational python landed IGNORED and unbacked-up
# until this line (card d7ac3470). A rule that needs a `git add -f` to obey is not a rule.
!store/*.py
# Stitch design-gen tools are operational scripts (tracked except node_modules).
!store/stitch-tools/gen.mjs
# The watched-repos registry is hand-maintained CONFIG, not runtime state -- nothing writes it (the
# watcher and both dashboard consumers only read), so tracking it causes no churn. It was ignored, and
# a security-relevant correction (repomix pin 1.17.0 -> 1.18.0, card 435e5083) therefore existed only
# on this disk: unversioned, unbacked-up, and a fresh checkout would have restored the stale pin.
# Contains no secrets -- verified; the token/secret word matches in it are prose. Card 8338cf69.
!store/watched-repos.json
# Canonical, hand-maintained CONFIG (the shared session-limit phrase list, card 115c21e7), not
# runtime state -- 6 scripts read it, nothing writes it. Same reasoning as watched-repos.json above:
# an unversioned copy would exist only on this disk and a fresh install would silently regress to
# the pre-consolidation drift. Named, not a blanket *.json rule, so runtime state under store/
# (quota-monitor-state.json, weekly-usage.json, ...) stays ignored.
!store/session-limit-pattern.json
!store/stitch-tools/fetch-pngs.mjs
!store/stitch-tools/package.json
# Gate-sweep scanners are operational scripts (named, not a blanket *.py rule,
# so future runtime .py data under store/ stays ignored).
!store/cybersec-gate-scan.py
!store/cybered-gate-scan.py
# Shape-based secret pre-filter the repomix pack path runs before packing (card 2f781b49).
!store/secret-shape-scan.py
!store/cleancore-landed-check.py
# gate-pretriage-card.sh's candidate-commit selection, extracted for independent testing (card 34e7285e).
!store/gate-pretriage-candidates.py
# The Firecrawl adoption decision (card 91c4a369): licence finding, key-handling shape and the
# acceptance procedure. Blocked on a key today, which is exactly why it must survive this disk --
# the next reader needs to know it was decided, not forgotten.
!store/firecrawl-adoption.md
# The CodeBurn policy (card 56ed32df) is a POLICY, not runtime data: it carries Peti's approved
# limits and the audited reasons for them (share/pair forbidden, and the always-share flag that
# re-exposes the machine from a plain `codeburn`). A prohibition that exists only on one disk is not
# a prohibition -- same argument as watched-repos.json above. Named, not a blanket *.md rule, so
# runtime markdown under store/ stays ignored.
!store/codeburn-usage-policy.md
# Local-LLM offload tooling (config + task templates) is operational, not runtime data.
!store/local-llm-model
!store/local-llm-skills/
!store/local-llm-skills/*.txt
workspace/
agents/
reports/
# CLAUDEIGN820: '.claude/' (directory pattern) stopped traversal, so the
# '!.claude/settings.json' negation never fired -- the tracked settings file
# was invisible as untracked and git add refused it on fresh clones.
# '.claude/*' lets git enumerate the first level so the negation can work;
# '*/**/.claude/' keeps nested .claude dirs ignored like before.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
*/**/.claude/
.config/

